    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d710a-53">

                <pb facs="0383" n="203" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg203"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">Editor’s Note</hi></head>
                <p>—No official record of the substance of this conversation has been found.
                        Stimson’s diary entry for July 21
                    contains the following summary: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I then left the ‘Little White House’, picked up Bundy, and went to the Prime Minister’s
                            house where we conferred with him and Lord
                                Cherwell. I turned over the paper<anchor n="1"
                                xml:id="d710a-53-f1"/> to Churchill and he began reading it but was interrupted a
                            few minutes before five in order to hurry to the Big Three Conference at
                            five o’clock. He asked me to return on the following morning to finish
                            up the report.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
